api.github.com/users/janakdr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2021-07-02T17:42:10Z","updated_at":"2021-07-13T14:46:35Z","closed_at":"2021-07-13T14:46:35Z","author_association":"MEMBER","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"While preparing a new Windows VM image, I noticed that there's one test method apparently consistently failing now:\r\n\r\n```\r\nExecuting tests from //src/test/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/skyframe:SkyframeTests\r\n[...]\r\nThere was 1 failure:\r\n1) testPropagatesRuntimeExceptions(com.google.devtools.build.lib.skyframe.FilesystemValueCheckerTest)\r\njava.lang.NullPointerException\r\n\tat com.google.common.truth.ThrowableSubject.hasMessageThat(ThrowableSubject.java:58)\r\n\tat com.google.devtools.build.lib.skyframe.FilesystemValueCheckerTest.testPropagatesRuntimeExceptions(FilesystemValueCheckerTest.java:1005)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe main differences between the old image and the new one are:\r\n- Windows version (old: Windows 10 build 1909, new: Windows 10 20H2)\r\n- Visual Studio Build Tools that provide e.g. the C++ compiler (old: 2017, new: 2019)\r\n- System JDK (old: Azul Zulu OpenJDK 8, new: Azul Zulu OpenJDK 11)\r\n- Windows SDK (old: v10.1, new: v2004)\r\n\r\nFull log is here: https://storage.googleapis.com/bazel-testing-buildkite-artifacts/c777f519-3c2c-4cf0-9c5b-14b2adb0f142/src%5Ctest%5Cjava%5Ccom%5Cgoogle%5Cdevtools%5Cbuild%5Clib%5Cskyframe%5CSkyframeTests%5Cattempt_1.log\r\n\r\nThis test method failed with this message even after three retries.\r\n\r\n@janakdr Any idea why this would fail with a NullPointerException? Unfortunately you can't yet easily test it yourself, as the new Windows VM image isn't live yet, but if you want to try a fix, I can help. Or we could disable the test method, roll the image out and then you could iterate on it until it works. Not sure if you're the right person, but saw that you touched the file recently. 😊 \r\n","closed_by":{"login":"bazel-io","id":15028808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io","html_url":"https://github.com/bazel-io","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/13638/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/13638/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}